---@field customAttributes? gcp.css_v1.CustomAttributeList A list of custom (CSS-provided) attributes. It can also be used for submitting any attribute of the feed specification in its generic form (for example: `{ "name": "size type", "value": "regular" }`). This is useful for submitting attributes not explicitly exposed by the API, such as additional attributes used for Buy on Google.
---@field freshnessTime? string DEPRECATED. Use expiration_date instead. Represents the existing version (freshness) of the CSS Product, which can be used to preserve the right order when multiple updates are done at the same time. This field must not be set to the future time. If set, the update is prevented if a newer version of the item already exists in our system (that is the last update time of the existing CSS products is later than the freshness time set in the update). If the update happens, the last update time is then set to this freshness time. If not set, the update will not be prevented and the last update time will default to when this request was received by the CSS API. If the operation is prevented, the aborted exception will be thrown.
---@field updateMask? string The list of CSS product attributes to be updated. If the update mask is omitted, then it is treated as implied field mask equivalent to all fields that are populated (have a non-empty value). Attributes specified in the update mask without a value specified in the body will be deleted from the CSS product. Update mask can only be specified for top level fields in attributes and custom attributes. To specify the update mask for custom attributes you need to add the `custom_attribute.` prefix. Providing special "*" value for full CSS product replacement is not supported.
---@field name string Identifier. The name of the CSS Product input. Format: `accounts/{account}/cssProductInputs/{css_product_input}`, where the last section `css_product_input` consists of 3 parts: contentLanguage~feedLabel~offerId. Example: accounts/123/cssProductInputs/de~DE~rawProvidedId123

---@class gcp.css_v1.PatchAccountsLabelsRequest
---@field displayName? string The display name of this label.
---@field labelType? gcp.css_v1.AccountLabelLabelTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of this label.
---@field accountId? string Output only. The ID of account this label belongs to.
---@field description? string The description of this label.
---@field labelId? string Output only. The ID of the label.
---@field name string Identifier. The resource name of the label. Format: accounts/{account}/labels/{label}

---The price represented as a number and currency.
---@class gcp.css_v1.Price
---@field currencyCode? string The currency of the price using three-letter acronyms according to [ISO 4217](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217).
---@field amountMicros? string The price represented as a number in micros (1 million micros is an equivalent to one's currency standard unit, for example, 1 USD = 1000000 micros).

---The product details.
---@class gcp.css_v1.ProductDetail
---@field attributeValue? string The value of the product detail.
---@field sectionName? string The section header used to group a set of product details.
---@field attributeName? string The name of the product detail.

---@alias gcp.css_v1.ProductDetailList gcp.css_v1.ProductDetail[]

---The dimension of the product.
---@class gcp.css_v1.ProductDimension
---@field value? number Required. The dimension value represented as a number. The value can have a maximum precision of four decimal places.
---@field unit? string Required. The dimension units. Acceptable values are: * "`in`" * "`cm`"

---The weight of the product.
---@class gcp.css_v1.ProductWeight
---@field unit? string Required. The weight unit. Acceptable values are: * "`g`" * "`kg`" * "`oz`" * "`lb`"
---@field value? number Required. The weight represented as a number. The weight can have a maximum precision of four decimal places.

---The group information for methods in the CSS API. The quota is shared between all methods in the group. Even if none of the methods within the group have usage the information for the group is returned.
---@class gcp.css_v1.QuotaGroup
---@field quotaLimit? string Output only. The maximum number of calls allowed per day for the group.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the quota group. Format: accounts/{account}/quotas/{group} Example: `accounts/12345678/quotas/css-products-insert` Note: The {group} part is not guaranteed to follow a specific pattern.
---@field quotaMinuteLimit? string Output only. The maximum number of calls allowed per minute for the group.
---@field methodDetails? gcp.css_v1.MethodDetailsList Output only. List of all methods group quota applies to.
---@field quotaUsage? string Output only. The current quota usage, meaning the number of calls already made on a given day to the methods in the group. The daily quota limits reset at 12:00 PM midday UTC.

---@alias gcp.css_v1.QuotaGroupList gcp.css_v1.QuotaGroup[]

---@alias gcp.css_v1.StringList string[]

---@class gcp.css_v1.UpdateLabelsAccountsRequest
---@field labelIds? gcp.css_v1.StringList The list of label IDs to overwrite the existing account label IDs. If the list is empty, all currently assigned label IDs will be deleted.
---@field parent? string Optional. Only required when updating MC account labels. The CSS domain that is the parent resource of the MC account. Format: accounts/{account}
---@field name string Required. The label resource name. Format: accounts/{account}

